Key Takeaway

Network Security Groups are a foundational Azure networking security service that controls traffic flowing into and out of Azure resources. By properly configuring NSGs, understanding rule processing, and leveraging Application Security Groups, Azure Administrators can build secure, scalable, and well-governed network architectures that protect organizational workloads and enforce least-privilege access principles.
